{
  "text": "2000A14 Discuss the roles of plasma esterases on drugs used in\nanaethesia.\nList:\n·\nEsterases\n·\nPlasma cholinesterase\n·\nRBC esterase\n·\nNon-specific plasma esterase\n·\n(Muscle esterase)\nEsterases:\nActivity\n·\nEster hydrolysis: ester -> acid + alcohol\nSource\n·\nMostly liver\nCapacity\n·\nHigh\nMetabolites\n·\nMostly inactive (exception: laudanosine ->\n  neurotoxicity)\nFactors\n↑\nactivity\n·\n↑temp\n·\n±\n↓pH (benzylisoquinoliniums)\nFactors\n↓\nactivity\n·\nDeficiency\n·\nDrug\n  inhibitors\nPlasma cholinesterase:\nDrugs metabolised\n·\nSuxamethonium\n·\nMivacurium\n·\nEster\n  local anaesthetics e.g. tetracaine\n·\nAcetylcholinesterases\n  e.g.neostigmine\nSux metabolism\n·\nSux\n  -> succinylmonocholine + choline\n·\nS’monocholine\n  -> succinic acid + choline\nRapid metabolism\n·\nRapid\n  offset of paralysis for sux (~5-10mins) and mivacurium\n·\nLower\n  risk of systemic toxicity with ester LAs (e.g. prilocaine IV for Bier’s\n  block)\nPolymorphism\n·\nTwo\n  copies\n·\nFour\n  types: usual, dibucaine-resistant (DR), chloride resistant, silent\n·\nUsual-usual:\n  (~96% population): dibucaine number (DN) 80, offset ~5 mins\n·\nUsual-DR:\n  (a few %): DN 60, offset ~30mins\n·\nDR-DR:\n  (<<1%): DN 20, offset 8-12 hours\nInhibition of production\n·\nDisease\n  states: heart failure, liver failure, renal failure, cancer\n·\nPregnancy:\n  same amount, higher blood volume hence lower concentration\nInhibition of activity\n·\nAcetylcholinesterase\n  inhibitors\n·\nOther\n  drugs: metoclopramide, ketamine, oral contraceptive pill, Lithium,\n  lignocaine, ester local anaesthetics, cytotoxics\nStimulation of production\n·\nObesity\n·\nAlcohol\n  abuse\nRBC esterase:\nDrug target\n·\nEsmolol (ester-methyl-olol)\nRapid rate\n·\nAccounts for short t\n1/2β\nof esmolol\n  10 mins\nNon-specific\nesterase:\nDrug targets\n·\nBenzylisoquinoliniums\n·\nRemifentanil\nBenzylisoquinolinium metabolism\n·\nAtracurium\n  -> monoquaternary alcohol + monoquaternary acid + laudanosine\n·\nIndependent\n  of kidney and liver, unlike aminosteroids\n·\nLess\n  important for cisatracurium\nRemifentanil\n·\nMetabolism\n  by non-specific esterases in plasma and tissue, especially muscle\n·\nOne\n  minimally active carboxylic acid metabolite (activates TLR-4 ->\n  hyperalgaesia)\n·\nAccounts\n  for very short max context sensitive half time (CSHT 10 min), hence suitable\n  for TIVA\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
